    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d876">

                <pb facs="0947" n="1781" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111N83/61</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Norway</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-24T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>435. While the Department prefers that representations to Norwegian Government
                    regarding the barrage should not be in the form of a joint action with your
                    British colleague, it is considered wise that you should acquaint him informally
                    and orally with the action <pb facs="0948" n="1782" xml:id="pg1782"/> you have
                    already taken and such other steps as you may be instructed to take in the
                    future.</p>
                <p>You should nevertheless intimate unofficially but very plainly to the British
                    Minister and others with whom you may discuss the matter that this Government is
                    not in sympathy with the course the British Government is taking as outlined in
                    the second paragraph of your 1040, August 21, 3 p.m., as it is important that
                    they should understand that this Government does not wish to act in a way which
                    can be construed as an infringement of the territorial sovereignty of
                    Norway.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
